Package: reditR
Type: Package
Title: Differential RNA Editing Analysis for Single-Cell Pseudobulk Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Saanvi",
           family = "Jiteendra",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sj1825@ic.ac.uk")
Description: Statistical tools for detecting differentially edited RNA sites
    in single-cell RNA-seq data aggregated by cluster (pseudobulk). Offers
    three independent significance tests -- a binomial generalised linear
    mixed model (GLMM), Fisher's exact test, and Wilcoxon rank-sum -- each
    run on all sites and independently FDR-corrected, so the user can pick
    whichever test suits their experimental design rather than trusting a
    single combined verdict. Designed for use downstream of editing-site
    detection pipelines such as SPRINT, working from per-site read-count
    tables. Includes simulation utilities for power analysis and method
    validation.
